/E (The Infrastructure Failure \(Atlanta 1996\): Atlanta saw minor pre-event price increases of 5-10%. However, the event ultimately had a negative long-term effect on immediate real estate prices in certain zones because the investments weren't properly integrated into an existing, long-term urban planning framework.)
